# RA + TEMPORAL-FILTER BD-RATE — port vs C reference (2026-09-24)

host:    lilith (WSL2 x86_64)
commit:  35e57f952 (MCTF-D tip — delayed-intra key path landed)
corpus:  pd-derf-720p 256x256, johnny / vidyo4 / fourpeople — each looped to
         9 frames so the encode is one key frame plus ONE COMPLETE 8-picture
         mini-GOP (hier 3)
config:  CQP p6, qp {25,40,55}, intra period 64, pred-struct RA, hier 3,
         temporal filtering ON (the default on both sides)
configs:
  rs   = port, SVT_PRED_STRUCT=2 SVTAV1_HIER_LEVELS=3 (enable_tf default)
  cra  = C reference v4.2.0, --hierarchical-levels 3 (--enable-tf default 1)

method:  per-frame PSNR-Y vs source after aomdec --rawvideo, averaged over
         the 9 displays; BD-rate = piecewise-linear integrate of
         log2(bytes) over the common PSNR range (3 qp points — honest
         ballpark, not a test-set claim). Same methodology as
         video_gap_bdrate_2026-09-23.

result (BD-rate, positive = port worse):
  clip        rs vs cra
  johnny        +0.37%
  vidyo4        -0.03%
  fourpeople    +0.55%

TF-engaged check (same cells, TF on vs off per side — positive = TF helps):
  clip        port notf-vs-tf   C notf-vs-tf
  johnny          +1.82%           +2.08%
  vidyo4          +2.59%           +3.17%
  fourpeople      +2.43%           +4.27%
  The port's filter captures 60-90% of C's TF benefit; the residual is the
  generic inter envelope (ME/MD divergence compounds over the filtered
  references), not a disabled or degenerate filter.

per-point notes:
  - qp25: the port spends MORE bits (+2%..+32%) at HIGHER PSNR (+0.1..+0.6dB)
  - qp55: the port spends FEWER bits (-10%..-23%) at LOWER PSNR (-0.8..-2.1dB)
  The qp55 divergence is bit-ALLOCATION, not filtering: C's hierarchical
  QP-offset ladder spends more on the leaf layer than the port does at high
  QP. BD-rate over the common PSNR range reads the real gap: sub-1%.

context: at the same corpus/config the flat low-delay port-vs-C parity is
  ±0.15% (video_gap_bdrate_2026-09-23). RA+TF lands within ~0.55% — the
  residual is the generic inter envelope (ME/MD divergence), not a TF defect:
  the delayed-intra key's recon moved from == C-noTF (unfiltered) to closer
  to C-TF than to C-noTF on the same clip (maxdiff 15 vs 23).

gates behind this landing: ra_selfcheck_gate.sh 11/11 (recon == aomdec on
  every display frame, hidden-frame anti-vacuity), workspace nextest
  4003/4003, regression_spotcheck 145/145.
